## Pricing (UI only, no real integration)
- Free: basic vault, 30–50 item limit, no ads.
- Pro one-time: about **249 TL / 7.99 USD**. Pro yearly: **449 TL**.
- The app is not sold on Gumroad. Gumroad would only carry a helper setup/privacy guide.
- No billing/IAP code yet (see `DECISIONS.md`). Real payment integration is a BLOCKER-level step.

## 3-week MVP plan (brief §2) and status (from PROGRESS.md / code, 2026-09-25)
The checkboxes in the brief are not ticked. Actual status:

**Week 1: security core (done)**
- Encrypted vault (key generation, secure storage, AES-GCM service)
- PIN create/verify/change (hash + salt, attempt limit + lockout)
- Biometric unlock with PIN fallback
- Auto-lock in background, FLAG_SECURE
- Gallery vault (import, encrypted copy, grid, viewer, delete, export)
- Unit tests for crypto and auth

**Week 2: entry layer and content (done)**
- Working calculator entry (type PIN, then `=`), disclosed in onboarding and the listing
- Optional decoy PIN that opens a separate empty vault
- Encrypted notes with search
- Onboarding with "own device only" confirmation
- TR + EN strings

**Week 3: virtual phone UI and Play prep (partly done)**
- Done:
  - Vault home icon grid with wallpapers
  - Settings: change PIN, biometrics, decoy PIN
  - Play prep docs: privacy policy, Data safety, TR/EN listing, minimal permission list
  - Release APK built (debug-signed)
- Not done yet:
  - In-app notification isolation (a notification list visible only inside the vault; no
    content in system notifications)
  - Pro/payment **UI stub**
  - Screenshots
  - Real release signing

**v0.2 additions:** calculator launcher label + original icon, and Second phone.
50 tests pass, `flutter analyze` is clean, and the arm64 release APK is built.
Second phone is **not yet tested on a real device**.

## Definition of done (end of week 3)
- App builds, and analyze and tests are clean.
- Every week 1–3 item is ticked, or explained in `BLOCKERS.md`.
- 3 weeks of PR history and an up-to-date `PROGRESS.md`.
- Play readiness pack (policy, Data safety, store listing) is in the repo.

